    "body": "Brings `lsp/clice.lua` up to date with the clice server.\n\n- `root_markers`: clice reads `clice.toml` and `compile_commands.json`; `compile_flags.txt` and `configure.ac` mean nothing to it. The workspace folder decides where clice looks for compilation databases and keeps its cache, so a subdirectory holding a `.clang-format` or `.clang-tidy` must not become it.\n- `capabilities`: `offsetEncoding` and `editsNearCursor` are clangd extensions; clice answers in UTF-16.\n- `filetypes`: clice handles CUDA.\n- `on_attach`: buffer-local commands for clice's compilation context requests (the source file a header compiles in, or the compile command of a source file listed with several) and its build configurations.\n\nThe same file is kept in the clice repository ([`editors/nvim/lsp/clice.lua`](https://github.com/clice-io/clice/blob/main/editors/nvim/lsp/clice.lua)), where a headless Nvim test runs the context commands against a real server.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-09T09:33:29Z",
    "comment_data": [],
